{{!-- Who is setting out, where they are bound, and which map is showing.

      SHARED BY BOTH SURFACES. The route step draws these above its map; the "See the whole map"
      window draws the same controls above its viewport, which is what makes the popout a peer of
      the panel rather than a picture of it. Context is the journey object from
      ExpeditionDialog._buildJourney.

      Every control is bound once, in that dialog's activateListeners, and the window forwards its
      own clicks to the very same methods — so "change the origin" cannot come to mean two
      different things depending on which window you did it in. --}}
<div class="stonetop-journey-picks">
  <label class="stonetop-journey-picklab">
    Setting out from
    <select class="stonetop-journey-origin">
      {{#each journey.originOptions}}
      <option value="{{slug}}"{{#if selected}} selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>
      {{/each}}
    </select>
  </label>
  {{#if journey.hasDestination}}
  <span class="stonetop-journey-bound">bound for <strong>{{journey.destination.name}}</strong></span>
  <button type="button" class="stonetop-journey-clear" data-tooltip="Clear the destination">
    <i class="fas fa-xmark"></i>
  </button>
  {{else}}
  <span class="stonetop-journey-bound stonetop-journey-bound--empty">Tap a place to set the destination.</span>
  {{/if}}
  {{!-- Put the way they go onto the table's own map. It sits with the DESTINATION rather than with
        the map tabs because it is an act on the journey, not a choice of picture: the scene it
        draws on is the one the reader is looking at, which need not be the map showing here.

        GM-only, and absent rather than disabled for a player: it writes a Scene flag, which a
        player cannot do, and a control that is visibly there and refuses on click is worse than
        one that never offered. Players still SEE the line, because the flag broadcasts. Built only
        once a destination is picked, for the same reason. See utils/scene-route.js. --}}
  {{#if journey.scene}}
  <button type="button" class="stonetop-journey-to-scene{{#if journey.scene.showing}} is-showing{{/if}}"
          data-tooltip="{{journey.scene.tooltip}}">
    <i class="fas {{journey.scene.icon}}"></i> {{journey.scene.label}}
  </button>
  {{/if}}
</div>

<div class="stonetop-journey-tiers" role="tablist" aria-label="Map">
  {{#each journey.tiers}}
  <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="{{isActive}}" data-tier="{{slug}}"
          class="stonetop-journey-tier{{#if isActive}} is-active{{/if}}">
    {{name}}{{#unless hasMap}} <i class="fas fa-image-slash" data-tooltip="Not imported"></i>{{/unless}}
  </button>
  {{/each}}
</div>
